IMPORT prelude

-- California Unemployment Insurance Code, Division 1, Part 1, Chapter 5 -- unemployment compensation benefits.
--
-- Edition: the Legislative Counsel's official bulk export (code tables updated 2026-10-03), deposited as unofficial plain
-- text at ../../registers/source-bundle/ca-uic-div1-part1-ch5-unemployment-compensation-benefits-2026-10.txt.
--
-- In: s 1252(a)(1), (2) (unemployed); s 1253(a)-(f) (weekly eligibility, the waiting week); s 1255.3(a), (c) (pension
-- offset); s 1256 (voluntary quit without good cause; discharge for misconduct; the presumption; the deemed good causes);
-- s 1257(b) (refusing suitable work); s 1260(a), (b) (how long a disqualification lasts); s 1279 (the payment for a week
-- with wages); s 1280(c) (the weekly benefit amount, new claims effective from 1 January 2005: the table and 50% / 13 to
-- $450); s 1281 (the base-period test; the maximum award); s 1327 (the last employer's 10 days to submit facts); s 1328
-- (30 days to appeal).
--
-- Out: claims effective before 2005 (`not covered`); s 1253.5 and the other special eligibility sections; s 1257(a) and
-- s 1260(c), (d) (false statements); s 1262 (trade disputes); s 1264 and the other special disqualifications; extended
-- duration benefits; the alternate base period (s 1275; the claimant states base-period wages); disability insurance (Part
-- 2, a separate subject).
--
-- Federal frame (not imported): FUTA, 26 U.S.C. 3304, and SSA Title III, in subjects/us/internal-revenue-code-of-1986 and
-- subjects/us/social-security-act. California does not tax these benefits (Rev. & Tax. Code 17083); they are federal gross
-- income (26 U.S.C. 85).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING, from the seat of the unemployed worker (the claimant). Expected values in the case file are
-- hand-written. No pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT ADVICE.

§ `Unemployment Insurance Code, Chapter 5 -- unemployment compensation benefits`

§§ `What this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- s 1280(a), (b), (c)(1)-(2): earlier claims used other tables and maximums
    `this encoding computes the weekly benefit amount for new claims effective on or after 1 January 2005 only`

DECLARE `Answer` IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `amount`  IS A NUMBER
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

-- ss 1279(b), 1280(c), 1281(c): amounts "computed to the next higher multiple of one dollar ($1)".
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`up to the dollar` MEANS
    IF FLOOR `amount` EQUALS `amount`
    THEN `amount`
    ELSE FLOOR `amount` PLUS 1

§§ `s 1280(c) -- the weekly benefit amount`

-- "the amount appearing in column B in the following table opposite the wage bracket in column A that contains the wages
-- paid to the individual ... during the quarter of his or her base period in which his or her wages were the highest".
-- The table runs from $900.00 ($40) to $1,832.99 ($70), each row one dollar more. Above $1,832.99, "50 percent of these
-- wages divided by 13, but in no case ... exceed ... (3) For new claims filed with an effective date beginning on or after
-- January 1, 2005, four hundred fifty dollars ($450)", raised to the next dollar. Below $900 the table has no row.
GIVEN `highest quarter wages` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the table amount` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1807.00 THEN 70   -- 1,807.00 to 1,832.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1768.00 THEN 69   -- 1,768.00 to 1,806.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1742.00 THEN 68   -- 1,742.00 to 1,767.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1703.00 THEN 67   -- 1,703.00 to 1,741.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1677.00 THEN 66   -- 1,677.00 to 1,702.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1638.00 THEN 65   -- 1,638.00 to 1,676.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1612.00 THEN 64   -- 1,612.00 to 1,637.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1586.00 THEN 63   -- 1,586.00 to 1,611.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1547.00 THEN 62   -- 1,547.00 to 1,585.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1521.00 THEN 61   -- 1,521.00 to 1,546.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1495.00 THEN 60   -- 1,495.00 to 1,520.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1456.00 THEN 59   -- 1,456.00 to 1,494.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1430.00 THEN 58   -- 1,430.00 to 1,455.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1404.00 THEN 57   -- 1,404.00 to 1,429.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1365.00 THEN 56   -- 1,365.00 to 1,403.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1339.00 THEN 55   -- 1,339.00 to 1,364.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1313.00 THEN 54   -- 1,313.00 to 1,338.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1287.00 THEN 53   -- 1,287.00 to 1,312.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1248.00 THEN 52   -- 1,248.00 to 1,286.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1222.00 THEN 51   -- 1,222.00 to 1,247.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1196.00 THEN 50   -- 1,196.00 to 1,221.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1170.00 THEN 49   -- 1,170.00 to 1,195.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1144.00 THEN 48   -- 1,144.00 to 1,169.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1118.00 THEN 47   -- 1,118.00 to 1,143.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1079.00 THEN 46   -- 1,079.00 to 1,117.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1053.00 THEN 45   -- 1,053.00 to 1,078.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1027.00 THEN 44   -- 1,027.00 to 1,052.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1001.00 THEN 43   -- 1,001.00 to 1,026.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 975.00 THEN 42   -- 975.00 to 1,000.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 949.00 THEN 41   -- 949.00 to 974.99
           IF `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 900.00 THEN 40   -- 900.00 to 948.99
           OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `highest quarter wages` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekly benefit amount` MEANS
    IF `highest quarter wages` GREATER THAN 1832.99
    THEN min 450 (`up to the dollar` ((50% TIMES `highest quarter wages`) DIVIDED BY 13))
    ELSE `the table amount` `highest quarter wages`

§§ `s 1281 -- the base-period test and the maximum award`

-- (a): no valid claim unless the highest quarter's wages were at least $1,300, or at least $900 with base-period wages of
-- 1.25 times the highest quarter.
GIVEN `highest quarter wages` IS A NUMBER, `base-period wages` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `can establish a valid claim` IF
        `highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 1300
    OR  (`highest quarter wages` AT LEAST 900 AND `base-period wages` AT LEAST (1.25 TIMES `highest quarter wages`))

-- (b), (c): the maximum in a benefit year is the lower of 26 times the weekly benefit amount and half the base-period
-- wages, raised to the next dollar.
GIVEN `weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER, `base-period wages` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum award` MEANS
    `up to the dollar` (min (26 TIMES `weekly benefit amount`) (`base-period wages` DIVIDED BY 2))

§§ `s 1252, s 1279 -- a week with some wages`

-- s 1252(a)(2): a week of less than full-time work counts as unemployment "if the wages payable ..., when reduced by
-- twenty-five dollars ($25) or 25 percent of the wages payable, whichever is greater, do not equal or exceed his or her
-- weekly benefit amount".
GIVEN `weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER, `wages for the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `unemployed in a week of part-time work` IF
    (`wages for the week` MINUS max 25 (25% TIMES `wages for the week`)) LESS THAN `weekly benefit amount`

-- s 1279(a): "his or her weekly benefit amount less the smaller of ... (1) The amount of wages in excess of twenty-five
-- dollars ($25) ... (2) The amount of wages in excess of 25 percent of the amount of wages"; (b) raised to the next dollar.
GIVEN `weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER, `wages for the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payment for the week` MEANS
    max 0 (`up to the dollar` (`weekly benefit amount` MINUS `the wages deducted` `wages for the week`))

GIVEN `wages for the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the wages deducted` MEANS
    min (max 0 (`wages for the week` MINUS 25)) (max 0 (`wages for the week` MINUS (25% TIMES `wages for the week`)))

-- s 1255.3(a), (c): reduced, not below zero, by a pension reasonably attributable to the week, only if under a plan
-- maintained or contributed to by a base-period or chargeable employer (and, for payments other than Social Security or
-- Railroad Retirement, as (c)(2) says, folded into the first fact here).
GIVEN `weekly payment` IS A NUMBER, `pension for the week` IS A NUMBER, `under a base-period employer's plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payment after a pension` MEANS
    IF `under a base-period employer's plan`
    THEN max 0 (`weekly payment` MINUS `pension for the week`)
    ELSE `weekly payment`

§§ `s 1253 -- eligibility for a week`

DECLARE `Week claimed` HAS
    `claim made for the week`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered and reporting for work`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `able and available for work`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `waiting week already served`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `searched for suitable work as instructed`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `took part in required reemployment activities, or had good cause` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 1253(a)-(f): eligible "only if the director finds" each condition. (d): the one-week waiting period, unless waived.
GIVEN w IS A `Week claimed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible for the week` IF
        w's `claim made for the week`
    AND w's `registered and reporting for work`
    AND w's `able and available for work`
    AND w's `waiting week already served`
    AND w's `searched for suitable work as instructed`
    AND w's `took part in required reemployment activities, or had good cause`

§§ `s 1256, s 1257(b), s 1260 -- disqualification`

DECLARE `How the job ended` IS ONE OF
    `laid off or let go for no misconduct`
    `quit with good cause`
    -- s 1256: "may be deemed" good cause: to accompany or join a spouse or domestic partner (including one whom marriage or
    -- partnership is imminent) where commuting is impractical; to protect the family or oneself from domestic violence
    `quit to follow a spouse or partner, or to escape domestic violence`
    -- s 1256: "shall be deemed": electing to be laid off in place of a less senior employee under a collective agreement;
    -- and retirement under a compulsory retirement clause is not leaving without good cause
    `quit by electing a seniority layoff, or compulsory retirement under a collective agreement`
    `quit without good cause`
    `discharged for misconduct connected with the work`

DECLARE `Effect of the separation` IS ONE OF
    `not disqualified`
    -- s 1260(a): ineligible from the week of the act "until they have, subsequent to the act ... and their registration
    -- for work, performed service in bona fide employment for which remuneration is received equal to or in excess of
    -- five times their weekly benefit amount"
    `disqualified until earning five times the weekly benefit amount in new work`

-- s 1256: the claimant "is presumed to have been discharged for reasons other than misconduct ... and not to have
-- voluntarily left ... without good cause unless his or her employer has given written notice to the contrary ... as
-- provided in Section 1327, setting forth facts sufficient to overcome the presumption". The director's finding is asked
-- as the category; the presumption only decides where the employer gave no such notice.
GIVEN `how` IS A `How the job ended`, `employer gave written notice overcoming the presumption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Effect of the separation`
`the effect of the separation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `quit without good cause` THEN
        IF `employer gave written notice overcoming the presumption`
        THEN `disqualified until earning five times the weekly benefit amount in new work`
        ELSE `not disqualified`
    WHEN `discharged for misconduct connected with the work` THEN
        IF `employer gave written notice overcoming the presumption`
        THEN `disqualified until earning five times the weekly benefit amount in new work`
        ELSE `not disqualified`
    OTHERWISE `not disqualified`

GIVEN `weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earnings needed to requalify` MEANS 5 TIMES `weekly benefit amount`

-- s 1257(b) with s 1260(b): refusing suitable work without good cause: "not less than 2 and no more than 10 consecutive
-- weeks" (the department chooses within that range).
GIVEN `weeks set by the department` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a lawful period for refusing suitable work` IF
    `weeks set by the department` AT LEAST 2 AND `weeks set by the department` AT MOST 10

§§ `Duties with deadlines`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the claimant`
    `the last employing unit`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `search for suitable work as instructed`
    `submit facts affecting the claimant's eligibility`
    `appeal to an administrative law judge`

-- s 1253(e): the week counts only if the claimant "conducted a search for suitable work in accordance with specific and
-- reasonable instructions of a public employment office". Days of the week claimed.
GIVEN `who` IS A `Party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the weekly work search` `who` MEANS
    PARTY `who`
    MUST  `search for suitable work as instructed`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `who` BECAUSE "s 1253(e): no search for suitable work as instructed; not eligible for the week"

-- s 1327: the employing unit notified of the claim "shall submit within 10 days after the mailing of the notice any facts
-- then known that may affect the claimant's eligibility" (extendable for good cause). For the claimant, this is what can
-- rebut the s 1256 presumption.
GIVEN `employer` IS A `Party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the employer's time to submit facts` `employer` MEANS
    PARTY `employer`
    MUST  `submit facts affecting the claimant's eligibility`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `employer` BECAUSE "s 1327: no facts submitted within 10 days of the notice"

-- s 1328: "The claimant and the employer may appeal from a determination or reconsidered determination to an
-- administrative law judge within 30 days from service of notice"; extendable for good cause.
GIVEN `who` IS A `Party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the right to appeal` `who` MEANS
    PARTY `who`
    MAY   `appeal to an administrative law judge`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- =====================================================================================================================
§ `Questions for the unemployed worker`

§§ `How much would I get?`

@export What is my California weekly unemployment benefit amount (Unemp. Ins. Code s 1280(c))? 0 means the table gives none.
GIVEN `my claim's effective year` IS A NUMBER @desc The year your new claim is effective (for example 2026)
      `my highest quarter wages` IS A NUMBER @desc Your wages in the quarter of your base period in which they were highest, in US dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer`
`What is my weekly benefit amount` MEANS
    IF `my claim's effective year` LESS THAN 2005
    THEN `not covered` `this encoding computes the weekly benefit amount for new claims effective on or after 1 January 2005 only`
    ELSE `answered` (`the weekly benefit amount` `my highest quarter wages`)

@export Have I earned enough in my base period to establish a California unemployment claim (Unemp. Ins. Code s 1281(a))?
GIVEN `my highest quarter wages` IS A NUMBER @desc Your wages in the highest quarter of your base period, in US dollars
      `my base-period wages` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total wages in the four quarters of your base period, in US dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I establish a claim` MEANS
    `can establish a valid claim` `my highest quarter wages` `my base-period wages`

@export What is the most California unemployment I can get in my benefit year (Unemp. Ins. Code s 1281(b))?
GIVEN `my weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly benefit amount, in US dollars
      `my base-period wages` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total base-period wages, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can get` MEANS
    `the maximum award` `my weekly benefit amount` `my base-period wages`

@export How much California unemployment will I be paid for a week in which I earned some wages (Unemp. Ins. Code ss 1252, 1279)?
GIVEN `my weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly benefit amount, in US dollars
      `my wages this week` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages (including self-employment and jury pay) payable to you for the week, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much will I be paid this week` MEANS
    IF `unemployed in a week of part-time work` `my weekly benefit amount` `my wages this week`
    THEN `the payment for the week` `my weekly benefit amount` `my wages this week`
    ELSE 0

@export How much is my weekly California unemployment payment after a pension is taken off (Unemp. Ins. Code s 1255.3)?
GIVEN `my weekly payment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly payment before the pension, in US dollars
      `my pension for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc The pension or annuity reasonably attributable to the week, in US dollars
      `the pension is from a base-period employer's plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid under a plan maintained or contributed to by an employer you worked for in your base period?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my payment after my pension` MEANS
    `the payment after a pension` `my weekly payment` `my pension for the week` `the pension is from a base-period employer's plan`

§§ `Am I eligible this week?`

@export Am I eligible for California unemployment benefits for this week (Unemp. Ins. Code s 1253)?
GIVEN `I filed my claim for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you certify (claim) for the week as required?
      `I am registered for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you registered for work and reporting as required?
      `I am able and available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you able to work and available for work that week?
      `I have served my waiting week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already served your one unpaid waiting week (or was it waived)?
      `I looked for work as instructed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you search for suitable work as the employment office instructed?
      `I did my reemployment activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were told to attend reemployment activities, did you (or did you have good cause not to)? Answer yes if not required.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I eligible this week` MEANS
    `eligible for the week` (`Week claimed` WITH
        `claim made for the week`                  IS `I filed my claim for the week`
        `registered and reporting for work`        IS `I am registered for work`
        `able and available for work`              IS `I am able and available`
        `waiting week already served`              IS `I have served my waiting week`
        `searched for suitable work as instructed` IS `I looked for work as instructed`
        `took part in required reemployment activities, or had good cause` IS `I did my reemployment activities`)

§§ `How my job ended`

@export Does the way my last job ended disqualify me from California unemployment benefits (Unemp. Ins. Code ss 1256, 1260(a))?
GIVEN `how my job ended` IS A `How the job ended` @desc How your most recent job ended: laid off or let go for no misconduct; quit with good cause; quit to follow a spouse or partner, or to escape domestic violence; quit by electing a seniority layoff, or compulsory retirement under a collective agreement; quit without good cause; discharged for misconduct connected with the work
      `my employer sent a written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer send EDD a written notice with facts showing you quit without good cause or were fired for misconduct?
GIVETH AN `Effect of the separation`
`Does how my job ended disqualify me` MEANS
    `the effect of the separation` `how my job ended` `my employer sent a written notice`

@export How much must I earn in new work to end a quit or misconduct disqualification (Unemp. Ins. Code s 1260(a))?
GIVEN `my weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly benefit amount, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much must I earn to requalify` MEANS
    `the earnings needed to requalify` `my weekly benefit amount`
